{
  "id": "is-subsequence",
  "questionId": "is-subsequence",
  "slug": "is-subsequence",
  "title": "Is Subsequence",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Two pointers",
  "patterns": [
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "you never need to look backward in t once you've matched a character - what does that suggest about how many pointers you need, and how they should move?",
    "keep one pointer in s and one in t; advance the t pointer every step, and only advance the s pointer when the characters match",
    "if the s pointer reaches the end of s, every character was matched in order - s is a subsequence",
    "if the t pointer runs out first, there weren't enough matching characters left in t"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "advancing the s pointer even when characters don't match",
    "not handling the empty-string case for s explicitly (though the two-pointer approach naturally handles it if written correctly)",
    "restarting the scan of t from the beginning for each character of s instead of continuing from where you left off"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings, `s` and `t`.\n\n**Determine whether `s` is a subsequence of `t`.**\n\nA subsequence means every character of `s` appears in `t` in the same\nrelative order, though not necessarily right next to each other.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= s.length <= 100",
      "0 <= t.length <= 10^4",
      "s and t consist of lowercase English letters and spaces"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "s is empty (always true)",
      "s is longer than t (always false, unless s is empty)",
      "s equals t exactly"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"abc\", t = \"ahbgdc\"",
        "output": "true",
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "explanation": "a, b, c appear in that order within ahbgdc, with other letters in between"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"axc\", t = \"ahbgdc\"",
        "output": "false",
        "expectedOutput": "false",
        "explanation": "there's no x anywhere in t"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"\", t = \"ahbgdc\"",
        "output": "true",
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "explanation": "an empty string is a subsequence of anything"
      }
    ],
